From: CEB-GNRD platform <ceb-gnrd@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] psu: consume CRPS devices selected during startup

CRPS identifies an externally managed slot, independently of the selected kernel
driver. Accept generic pmbus hwmon telemetry alongside megcrps800, and avoid
creating or deleting these clients when psusensor restarts. Other platforms
using the ordinary pmbus configuration retain their existing ownership.
Base: dbus-sensors 17f2fc3fe1400bf9e45c075e4864cc79afa2ed91 plus board patches 0001-0012.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD PSU integration]

diff --git a/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp b/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
--- a/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
+++ b/src/psu/PSUSensorMain.cpp
@@ -140,6 +140,7 @@
     {"PLI1209BC", I2CDeviceType{"pli1209bc", true}},
     {"pmbus", I2CDeviceType{"pmbus", true}},
     {"MEGCRPS800", I2CDeviceType{"megcrps800", true}},
+    {"CRPS", I2CDeviceType{"pmbus", true}},
     {"PXE1610", I2CDeviceType{"pxe1610", true}},
     {"Q54SN120A1", I2CDeviceType{"q54sn120a1", true}},
     {"Q54SW120A7", I2CDeviceType{"q54sw120a7", true}},
diff --git a/src/DeviceMgmt.hpp b/src/DeviceMgmt.hpp
--- a/src/DeviceMgmt.hpp
+++ b/src/DeviceMgmt.hpp
@@ -140,11 +140,17 @@
 
             std::optional<I2CDeviceParams> params =
                 getI2CDeviceParams(sensorTypes, cfg);
-            // The CEB-GNRD hotplug monitor exclusively owns these devices.
+            // CEB-GNRD PSU startup detection exclusively owns these devices.
             // Consume their hwmon files without creating/deleting I2C clients.
-            if (params.has_value() && params->type.name == "megcrps800")
+            if (params.has_value())
             {
-                continue;
+                const auto* type =
+                    std::get_if<std::string>(&cfg.at("Type"));
+                if (params->type.name == "megcrps800" ||
+                    (type != nullptr && *type == "CRPS"))
+                {
+                    continue;
+                }
             }
             if (params.has_value() && !params->deviceStatic())
             {
